    {
      "id": 22,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -520,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        460,
        520
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 21,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note: Kroma",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Kroma (Krea 2 finetune)\n\nSettings from the Kroma prompting study: 8 steps, CFG 1, euler / simple, zeroed negative, 1216x832. Prompt: quality prefix, medium first, text clause, key concept repeated at the end.\n\nRTX 5070 Laptop: plain 16 s, Automatic (3 stages, \u0394 0.05) 12 s, Manual (0.5x to step 4) 11-12 s.\n\n## SPEED on an image model\n\nAll SPEED nodes here have **model_type = image**. The sampler input comes from KSamplerSelect (euler).\n\n1. **Harvest** (muted): unmute it, run once, and read the report. Paste `noise_amplitude` and\n   `noise_decay_exponent` into the Automatic node. The values already in it were harvested from this\n   prompt and seed on an RTX 5070 Laptop.\n2. **SPEED Automatic** (active): stage boundaries come from the Harvest fit and `Tolerance (Delta)`.\n   At \u0394 0.005 the low-resolution stage ends in the first steps, so it saves little; \u0394 0.05 is the\n   useful setting for images.\n3. **SPEED Manual** (muted): fixed boundary, half resolution to step 4, then full resolution.\n   Unmute it and mute Automatic to use it instead.\n\n**Plain reference** (muted) is the same graph on SamplerCustomAdvanced, for comparison.\nSPEED changes the composition at a given seed (the low-resolution stage gets its own noise), so compare\nlooks, not pixels.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    }
  ],
